00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Tell me about the code word

614
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,000
That came from a Fillmont conference

615
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:58,000
and the troop had this code word, CFD,

616
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:01,000
which stands for confusion, frustration and danger.

617
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Their rationale was that those are the only three times

618
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:08,000
that adult leaders should interfere with youth leaders

619
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,000
And they used it as a code.

620
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:13,000
so if one leader saw another leader

621
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:16,000
sort of overstepping his bounds,

622
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:18,000
he just had to walk past him and say CFD,

623
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:20,000
And that was enough to remind the guy.

624
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,000
oh, I didn't need to do that,

625
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,000
They could have figured it out for themselves.

626
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:25,000
Nobody was going to get hurt.

627
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:28,000
What would constitute an intervention would be

628
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:31,000
if they were just totally confused about something,

629
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:34,000
if they had grown really, really frustrated with it

630
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:37,000
and it was getting to the point where it wasn't constructive

631
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:39,000
for them, or if it was dangerous.

632
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Right,

633
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:44,000
That's actually a pretty succinct way to triage a situation.

634
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,000
I like that

635
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:47,000
And if you do this for long enough,

636
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:50,000
the ninth method time the scouts will pick this up.

